  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1996-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sum of \\(1\\) through \\(11\\) is \\(66.\\) For ten numbers to average \\(6.1,\\) their sum must be \\(10 \\cdot 6.1 = 61.\\)\n\nSo the removed number is \\(66 - 61 = 5.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "The eleven numbers add up to \\(66\\)",
        "Ten numbers averaging \\(6.1\\) must total \\(61;\\) find what was removed"
      ],
